# The snapshot the models actually transcribe.
#
# Every published result in this repository is a statement about THIS snapshot and no
# other. It is the answer to "which version of the protocol was verified?", and it is
# deliberately a separate fact from "which snapshots have been vendored."
#
# Vendoring a newer snapshot does NOT move this. It moves only after the models have been
# re-validated against the newer text, and moving it is the LAST step of that work. A pin
# that advances when someone copies files in would quietly convert "we vendored the new
# spec" into "we verified the new spec," which are not the same claim and differ by
# roughly the entire cost of the project.
#
# Read by tools/spec-drift.py (`make specdrift`), which reports the distance between this
# snapshot and the live spec.
#
# One line, the directory name under spec-data/, no leading path.

v0.8.0
